  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of Cash Assistance to Mitigate the Risk of Forced Relocation of IDPs in Abyei Administrative Areas</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Thousands of people in Abyei town in South Sudan had to leave their homes because of violence between different groups in February and March 2022. Many of them are staying with the local community on private land in two sites in Nyinkuach and Bubchok. The landowners agreed to let the people stay there until December 2022, but now they want them to leave. The Government plans to relocate the people to Titie, a village near Abyei center and the UNISFA checkpoint. This project is providing urgent multisector support to the people through cash assistance. This includes money for transportation and other needs that helps the targeted internally displaced persons (IDPs) move to other locations and reduce the risk of conflict between them and the host community.</narrative>
  </description>
